====Usage notes====
As England has always constituted the most populous and important of the kingdoms comprising the United Kingdom, it has historically been used [[metonymously]] for the UK as a whole in English and (in translation) other languages as well. This usage is now considered uninformed or insulting, particularly to subjects of the other parts of the UK. The 1746 {{w|Wales and Berwick Act 1746|Wales & Berwick Act}} formalized the previous informal understanding that laws referencing the Kingdom of England alone also applied to the Principality of Wales; this continued to be the case until the 1967 {{w|Welsh Language Act 1967|Welsh Language Act}} required that any similarly general laws afterwards must specify England and Wales separately.

